  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/dba90d9fc6f17599a41cd301247ec604726adb3454a4cee740c639d64c40618f.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $x$-axis.\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-sin\u2061x.$\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\nsin\u2061(-x)=-sin\u2061x\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=sin\u2061(-x).$ However, $y=sin\u2061(-x)$ is not among the given options.",
